# ---- Model weights (40 GB) — fetched by fetch-models.sh, never committed ----
backend/models/

# ---- Vendored third-party checkouts (each carries its own .git) ----
cuda-samples/
# NVIDIA/skills
# ---- Virtualenvs ----
training/.venv/
**/.venv/

# ---- Runtime output: logs, screenshots, generated images ----
run/
backend/output/

# ---- Vendored Swagger UI assets ----
site/swagger-ui-bundle.js
site/swagger-ui.css

# ---- Junk ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak
*.log

# ---- Trained adapter weights (244 MB) — artifacts, not source ----
*.safetensors
*.gguf
training/adapter/tokenizer.json
training/adapter-qwen36/tokenizer.json

# ---- Nested third-party checkouts (belt and braces: these carry their own .git) ----
/cuda-samples
# ---- Reference trees added for the IPTV and Miner surfaces (third-party, large) ----
# Projects_Crypto alone is ~2.5 GB of Antminer/Braiins firmware images.
/cuda-programming-guide.pdf
__MACOSX/

# Vendored design reference for the image page restyle

# ---- Third-party engines we build and ship (contrib) vs read-only material ----
# contrib/ holds source we compile and run; references/ holds material we only read.
/contrib

# ---- Reference material, all third-party, consolidated under one directory ----
# Everything here is somebody else's code or a saved document kept for reference.
# ~8.5 GB, none of it ours, none of it tracked.
/references

# ---- Browser "Save page as" captures ----
# site/ is a staging directory that deploy.sh publishes wholesale. An 11.6 MB .mhtml and
# its .pdf print were saved into it to show a broken deploy, and a `git add -A` put both in
# a commit. deploy.sh now filters by extension; this keeps them out of the repo as well.
site/*.mhtml
site/*.pdf

# the snapshots moved out of site/ -- keep them on disk, not in the repo
docs/archive/site-snapshot-*/

# ---- Agent worktrees ----
# Claude Code creates isolated git worktrees under here. Four of them held 105 MB across
# 1,407 files, and each is a checkout of this same repo -- so a `git add -A` from the root
# would try to commit a second copy of the tree into itself. Remove a stale one with
# `git worktree remove --force .claude/worktrees/<name>`, never with rm -rf, or git keeps
# the registration and `git worktree list` lies to the next agent.
.claude/worktrees/

# ---- Session scratch ----
# Neither of these is source. q.json is a hand-built request body for probing the tuner
# guide; claudesessioninterrupted is a partial tool call captured when a session died.
/q.json
.claude/claudesessioninterrupted

# Contract signing private keys. The public half (contract-signing.pub) ships and is
# tracked; the private half must never be committed, never be on a rig, and never be in
# the environment of a web process. Belt and braces -- issue.py also chmods it 0600.
*.key
!contrib/**/*.key
backend/apps/licensing/contract-signing.key

# ---- Agent scratch, not source ----
# .claude/claudesessioninterrupted is a 271 KB dump of one interrupted session's transcript,
# written by the harness. HANDOVER.md is the state document by house rule ("do not create a
# second state document"); a raw transcript beside it is a second one that nobody maintains.
.claude/claudesessioninterrupted

# q.json is a scratch request body left at the repo root from hand-testing the tuner's guide
# endpoint. Nothing reads it -- a grep across the tree finds no reference.
/q.json

# ---- Live agent worktrees ----
# .claude/worktrees/ holds real `git worktree` checkouts (138 MB, four of them as this was
# written), each on its own branch with its own agent working inside it. Committing them
# into the main tree would nest a checkout inside its own repository -- and they are not
# source in any case, they are other branches' working copies. `git worktree list` is how
# you enumerate them; `git worktree remove` is how they go away.
.claude/worktrees/

# Rust build output for symon-gateway. Hundreds of megabytes of compiled dependencies, and
# `cargo build` reproduces all of it from Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock. Cargo.lock IS tracked --
# it is a binary that gets deployed, so the exact dependency versions matter.
symon-gateway/target/

# The compiled Go validator. Built by `make build-wasm`; see ops/middleware/limiter.go.
ops/middleware/*.wasm
